# Implementation Report

**Guiding principle:** Report only information that helps the developer understand what changed and what remains to be done.

After completing each implementation task, provide a concise report with **only** these sections:

## Implementation Summary

3–8 bullet points describing what was implemented.

## Files Modified

- New files
- Modified files
- Deleted files (if any)

Include a one-line description of the purpose of each important file.

## Tests

- Tests added
- Tests executed
- Test results

## Design Changes

If the implementation required changes to the design:

- Describe the change.
- Identify the affected section of `design.md`.

Otherwise state: **No design changes.**

## Remaining TODOs

List known limitations or follow-up work discovered during implementation.

If none: **None.**
